# Source footage and stills live on disk only — ~1 GB of camera material that
# has no business in git. The animation reads them by path; it never needs them
# committed. Keep them backed up separately.
#
# These rules only bind UNTRACKED files: the media was committed anyway and had
# to be removed from the index with `git rm --cached` before they took effect.
# It is still in history — see the repo's open item on rewriting that.
/*.mp4
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.JPG

# Video editor scratch
widevideo/cache/

# Render intermediates: 840 PNGs per pass, regenerated by `npm run render`.
animation/intro/frames/

# Footage plates: the live-action frames the intro composites over, pulled out
# of the source clips by `npm run plates`. ~400 MB and fully regenerable, but
# only on a machine that has the source footage.
animation/intro/plates/

# The rendered intro. It used to be tracked, back when it was 3 MB of pure
# graphics and worth having in a fresh clone. Once real footage went into the
# render it became ~90 MB of churn — a fresh blob in history on every pass —
# which is the exact habit that put 1.5 GB into this repo's history once
# already. It is fully regenerable: `npm run plates && npm run render`.
animation/intro/mliniste-intro.mp4

node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Local Claude Code permission allowlist — machine-specific, not shared config.
.claude/settings.local.json
